      "definition": "h = eta / (beta_star * max(lambda_0_star_max, 1))",
      "reason": "What must stay of order one is h beta_star times the whitened covariance, which is largest at the initialization whenever C_0 overshoots C_star. Two other scales each fail on one family. A multiple of the certified step 1/(2 beta_star lambda_max_star) carries the worst-case growth allowance lambda_max_star >= 1/alpha_star, never attained on the whitened log-cosh cells, so its conservatism grows like kappa_star and a multiplier chosen at kappa_star = 11 diverges at kappa_star = 2. A multiple of 1/beta_star alone ignores the initialization and diverges on the logistic posteriors, where C_0 overshoots C_star by two orders of magnitude. The scale used is the certified step with the non-attained growth allowance removed and the initialization kept."
